America's 250th anniversary.

00:12:43.699 --> 00:12:49.499
And you even mastered some new material

00:12:46.499 --> 00:12:50.699
such as the one and only YMCA. You do it

00:12:49.499 --> 00:12:52.299
very well.

00:12:50.699 --> 00:12:53.499
That's become quite successful. You

00:12:52.299 --> 00:12:55.499
know, that was

00:12:53.499 --> 00:12:56.999
32 years ago. That was number five.

00:12:55.499 --> 00:12:58.999
Didn't hit number one.

00:12:56.999 --> 00:13:01.099
But for many months it was number one.

00:12:58.999 --> 00:13:03.199
So it was 32. The difference was they

00:13:01.099 --> 00:13:04.999
got a little bit heavier

00:13:03.199 --> 00:13:06.899
as a band. The band it looked a little

00:13:04.999 --> 00:13:08.399
bit different, not totally recognizable,

00:13:06.899 --> 00:13:10.799
but they're great guys and they loved

00:13:08.399 --> 00:13:12.099
it. They weigh a couple of pounds more

00:13:10.799 --> 00:13:14.899
than they did.

00:13:12.099 --> 00:13:16.499
But uh it went from number five, which

00:13:14.899 --> 00:13:18.099
was a big hit, but it was number five.

00:13:16.499 --> 00:13:19.699
Didn't hit number one.

00:13:18.099 --> 00:13:21.899
But it hit number one for a long time

00:13:19.699 --> 00:13:23.499
with us. So when you think of it, it's

00:13:21.899 --> 00:13:25.499
pretty amazing, right? That a song you'd

00:13:23.499 --> 00:13:27.399
bring it back and it became

00:13:25.499 --> 00:13:29.299
a smash, which tells you the power of

00:13:27.399 --> 00:13:30.999
politics, doesn't it?

00:13:29.299 --> 00:13:33.099
And next month we're looking forward to

00:13:30.999 --> 00:13:35.699
having the President's own perform for

00:13:33.099 --> 00:13:39.099
dozens of top world leaders when they

00:13:35.699 --> 00:13:40.499
host the G20 conference in Florida in

00:13:39.099 --> 00:13:41.999
Doral.

00:13:40.499 --> 00:13:44.699
And it's going to be great. We have all

00:13:41.999 --> 00:13:46.199
the the top 20 leaders in the world

00:13:44.699 --> 00:13:49.899
going to be there.

00:13:46.199 --> 00:13:52.499
So it's a true honor to have you perform

00:13:49.899 --> 00:13:54.099
for us. You know, when I when I said the

00:13:52.499 --> 00:13:55.299
money we didn't think about this. I only

00:13:54.099 --> 00:13:56.099
said it this morning. I said, what are

00:13:55.299 --> 00:13:58.099
we going to do? Well, you're just going

00:13:56.099 --> 00:13:59.199
to have a minor ceremony.

00:13:58.099 --> 00:14:01.099
And I want to thank Chamberlain,

00:13:59.199 --> 00:14:03.099
wherever she may be, cuz she put this

00:14:01.099 --> 00:14:04.499
all together very quickly.

00:14:03.099 --> 00:14:06.399
And I said, well, are they going to

00:14:04.499 --> 00:14:07.599
play? No, they weren't. I said, wait a

00:14:06.399 --> 00:14:09.699
minute, I'm giving them a lot of money.

00:14:07.599 --> 00:14:11.599
We're going to up it to 500,000. Let

00:14:09.699 --> 00:14:13.499
them make like let them play a little

00:14:11.599 --> 00:14:14.699
music. Do you agree?

00:14:13.499 --> 00:14:16.301
So uh

00:14:14.699 --> 00:14:18.601
this was all sort of put together. Then

00:14:16.301 --> 00:14:20.801
I said, let's invite the press. So we

00:14:18.601 --> 00:14:23.401
actually invited the press. Often times

00:14:20.801 --> 00:14:26.101
not my favorite people, but that's okay.

00:14:23.401 --> 00:14:29.501
And they were all excited and we have

00:14:26.101 --> 00:14:32.401
really very some good stuff done by your

00:14:29.501 --> 00:14:34.801
your commissary, by people that love you

00:14:32.401 --> 00:14:36.801
and they love making good food for you.

00:14:34.801 --> 00:14:38.801
So I want you to know that we're very

00:14:36.801 --> 00:14:41.801
grateful and that

00:14:38.801 --> 00:14:44.001
John Philip Sousa famously said

00:14:41.801 --> 00:14:47.201
and wanted his own orchestra to be as

00:14:44.001 --> 00:14:48.701
great among bands as any there are in

00:14:47.201 --> 00:14:50.301
America.

00:14:48.701 --> 00:14:52.001
And he said it and you know what that's

00:14:50.301 --> 00:14:54.201
turned out to be true because friends of

00:14:52.001 --> 00:14:56.001
mine that are in the music business said

00:14:54.201 --> 00:14:57.901
that were here that night,

00:14:56.001 --> 00:15:00.201
but at other times also they said they

00:14:57.901 --> 00:15:03.001
are as good as it gets. So it's a big

00:15:00.201 --> 00:15:04.501
deal. So we put this together and I said

00:15:03.001 --> 00:15:05.801
to Dana, we got to make them work a

00:15:04.501 --> 00:15:07.501
little bit. So they're going to play a

00:15:05.801 --> 00:15:09.001
few songs for us.

00:15:07.501 --> 00:15:11.201
And

00:15:09.001 --> 00:15:12.901
it's something that everybody here, we

00:15:11.201 --> 00:15:14.401
have the cabinet here.

00:15:12.901 --> 00:15:16.601
We have the leaders here. We have a lot

00:15:14.401 --> 00:15:18.101
of generals here, a lot of great

00:15:16.601 --> 00:15:20.701
We have two great admirals here that I

00:15:18.101 --> 00:15:22.701
know and respect and we're doing so

00:15:20.701 --> 00:15:24.201
well. They've got that great talent for

00:15:22.701 --> 00:15:26.001
something else. It's called warfare,

00:15:24.201 --> 00:15:27.901
which is what we want.

00:15:26.001 --> 00:15:29.601
So now I'd like to ask my friend Dana

00:15:27.901 --> 00:15:31.201
White, one of the true legends, the most

00:15:29.601 --> 00:15:33.601
successful

00:15:31.201 --> 00:15:35.201
promoter of fights, but really I think I

00:15:33.601 --> 00:15:37.301
could say the most successful promoter

00:15:35.201 --> 00:15:39.301
of anything, frankly.

00:15:37.301 --> 00:15:41.301
What he's been able to do is really

00:15:39.301 --> 00:15:42.601
incredible and then I'm going to hand

00:15:41.301 --> 00:15:45.501
out the

00:15:42.601 --> 00:15:46.701
check along with Dana to director Ryan

00:15:45.501 --> 00:15:48.801
Nolen.

00:15:46.701 --> 00:15:50.801
And Dana, if you could

00:15:48.801 --> 00:15:52.401
come forward and say a few words, I'd

00:15:50.801 --> 00:15:55.301
love to listen. I could listen to this

00:15:52.401 --> 00:15:57.301
guy all day because he's an inspiration.

00:15:55.301 --> 00:15:58.601
He's an inspiration, respected by

00:15:57.301 --> 00:16:00.601
everybody,

00:15:58.601 --> 00:16:01.901
respected by the toughest people in the

00:16:00.601 --> 00:16:03.601
world because I think they might be the

00:16:01.901 --> 00:16:05.501
toughest. You don't get any tougher than

00:16:03.601 --> 00:16:07.701
them. But

00:16:05.501 --> 00:16:10.301
everybody loves and respects Dana White.

00:16:07.701 --> 00:16:10.301
Thank you, Dana.

00:16:11.376 --> 00:16:13.396
>> [applause]

00:16:15.801 --> 00:16:21.002
>> Thank you, Mr. President.

00:16:18.202 --> 00:16:23.902
This band prepared for Freedom

00:16:21.002 --> 00:16:26.602
250 like it was a military operation.

00:16:23.902 --> 00:16:29.602
Eight weeks of planning, 39 songs from

00:16:26.602 --> 00:16:31.302
32 different artists, many with custom

00:16:29.602 --> 00:16:33.902
arrangements, and

00:16:31.302 --> 00:16:36.102
in the days before the event, they spent

00:16:33.902 --> 00:16:38.402
four full days rehearsing with our

00:16:36.102 --> 00:16:40.602
production in the blazing sun and

00:16:38.402 --> 00:16:42.602
humidity here in DC.

00:16:40.602 --> 00:16:43.602
My head of production Craig Borsari said

00:16:42.602 --> 00:16:45.402
that

00:16:43.602 --> 00:16:47.902
when they would take breaks, these guys

00:16:45.402 --> 00:16:50.002
were in full military dress rehearsing

00:16:47.902 --> 00:16:51.702
in the sun. When they would get up, the

00:16:50.002 --> 00:16:53.402
seats were soaked.

00:16:51.702 --> 00:16:54.902
No complaints, not one complaint the

00:16:53.402 --> 00:16:56.102
entire time.

00:16:54.902 --> 00:16:57.902
Now, I've worked with a lot of great

00:16:56.102 --> 00:17:00.102
teams, and I know what it looks like

00:16:57.902 --> 00:17:01.802
when people take pride in their work. I

00:17:00.102 --> 00:17:03.302
saw it in the way the Marines handled

00:17:01.802 --> 00:17:05.302
every rehearsal,

00:17:03.302 --> 00:17:08.102
and I heard it in every song that was

00:17:05.302 --> 00:17:09.702
played at Freedom 250.

00:17:08.102 --> 00:17:11.502
There were times, like the President

00:17:09.702 --> 00:17:14.002
said,

00:17:11.502 --> 00:17:16.102
a song would be playing, and I would go,

00:17:14.002 --> 00:17:17.602
is that the DJ? Is the DJ playing? And

00:17:16.102 --> 00:17:19.502
you look over,

00:17:17.602 --> 00:17:22.402
and it was the band. And it sounded

00:17:19.502 --> 00:17:24.102
exactly like the artist.

00:17:22.402 --> 00:17:25.302
Uh it was it was really amazing. And I

00:17:24.102 --> 00:17:27.502
want to thank

00:17:25.302 --> 00:17:30.302
uh [snorts] Lieutenant Colonel Ryan

00:17:27.502 --> 00:17:33.202
Nalen. I want to thank Lieutenant

00:17:30.302 --> 00:17:35.802
Colonel Douglas Beryan,

00:17:33.202 --> 00:17:38.002
Gunnery Sergeant Scott Nimner, and every

00:17:35.802 --> 00:17:40.802
musician and crew member who helped pull

00:17:38.002 --> 00:17:44.302
this off, including those who joined us

00:17:40.802 --> 00:17:46.002
from Army, Navy, and Air Force.

00:17:44.302 --> 00:17:47.002
Now, a couple things I want to point out

00:17:46.002 --> 00:17:48.502
that are

00:17:47.002 --> 00:17:51.002
truly incredible.

00:17:48.502 --> 00:17:53.802
The album is available. The UFC Freedom

00:17:51.002 --> 00:17:57.302
250 album is available worldwide, and it

00:17:53.802 --> 00:17:59.452
has 4 million streams right now.

00:17:57.302 --> 00:18:01.202
Now, we have a big music department

00:17:59.452 --> 00:18:04.302
[snorts] at TKR our company. We have the

00:18:01.202 --> 00:18:05.902
WWE and the UFC, and we use a lot of

00:18:04.302 --> 00:18:08.502
music.

00:18:05.902 --> 00:18:11.802
And my music guys are telling me the

00:18:08.502 --> 00:18:14.202
fact that UFC Freedom 250 music made it

00:18:11.802 --> 00:18:15.502
to the first round of voting in the

00:18:14.202 --> 00:18:18.202
Grammys

00:18:15.502 --> 00:18:20.203
for album of the year is absolutely

00:18:18.202 --> 00:18:22.003
unbelievable and incredible. So,

00:18:20.203 --> 00:18:24.403
congratulations

00:18:22.003 --> 00:18:25.403
to you Marines. And like the President

00:18:24.403 --> 00:18:27.103
said,

00:18:25.403 --> 00:18:29.303
I hope you guys win. It would be

00:18:27.103 --> 00:18:31.603
absolutely incredible.

00:18:29.303 --> 00:18:33.303
Um, so on behalf of everybody at the

00:18:31.603 --> 00:18:35.503
UFC,

00:18:33.303 --> 00:18:37.603
thank you for the hours you put in.

00:18:35.503 --> 00:18:40.503
Thank you for your service and thank you

00:18:37.603 --> 00:18:42.703
for giving UFC Freedom 250 a sound of

00:18:40.503 --> 00:18:44.903
its own. It's been an absolute honor to

00:18:42.703 --> 00:18:48.203
work with you.

00:18:44.903 --> 00:18:48.203
Now I would like Thank you.

00:18:50.703 --> 00:18:55.803
Now I'd like to introduce Lieutenant

00:18:52.403 --> 00:18:55.803
Colonel Ryan Nalen.

00:18:57.748 --> 00:18:59.768
>> [applause]

