[applause]

00:19:09.003 --> 00:19:13.003
>> Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.

00:19:10.403 --> 00:19:15.203
Mr. President, Mr. White, thank you very

00:19:13.003 --> 00:19:17.703
much for your generosity and for your

00:19:15.203 --> 00:19:20.003
continued support of this incredible

00:19:17.703 --> 00:19:21.403
organization. Commandant, thank you for

00:19:20.003 --> 00:19:23.003
your support and being here. Speaker

00:19:21.403 --> 00:19:24.303
Johnson, you honor us with your

00:19:23.003 --> 00:19:26.703
presence.

00:19:24.303 --> 00:19:29.803
Mr. Secretary, appreciate your support

00:19:26.703 --> 00:19:31.903
as well. And uh Secretary uh Cao, thank

00:19:29.803 --> 00:19:35.103
you for being here. Friends, Marine

00:19:31.903 --> 00:19:37.903
Band, this party is for you.

00:19:35.103 --> 00:19:40.303
We are so grateful for the opportunity

00:19:37.903 --> 00:19:42.503
to perform for you today, Mr. President.

00:19:40.303 --> 00:19:45.603
We're so grateful for your continued

00:19:42.503 --> 00:19:47.303
support of music, the arts, and the

00:19:45.603 --> 00:19:49.503
United States Marine Band. We have a

00:19:47.303 --> 00:19:50.903
special program that we've put together

00:19:49.503 --> 00:19:54.103
for you.

00:19:50.903 --> 00:19:55.803
This organization dates back to 1798,

00:19:54.103 --> 00:19:57.803
the beginnings of our country, as the

00:19:55.803 --> 00:19:59.303
President said. And the thing that I

00:19:57.803 --> 00:20:01.203
love most, if I had to pick something I

00:19:59.303 --> 00:20:03.503
love most about the United States Marine

00:20:01.203 --> 00:20:06.203
Band, is when I hear them play,

00:20:03.503 --> 00:20:08.103
it's an unbroken lineage. The people

00:20:06.203 --> 00:20:10.303
that you hear playing have played with

00:20:08.103 --> 00:20:12.503
people who have played with people who

00:20:10.303 --> 00:20:14.303
have played for John Philip Sousa, who

00:20:12.503 --> 00:20:15.603
played to the founding of our country.

00:20:14.303 --> 00:20:17.303
And if you think about how you learn

00:20:15.603 --> 00:20:20.103
music

00:20:17.303 --> 00:20:22.303
and play in an ensemble, you sit and you

00:20:20.103 --> 00:20:25.005
have the music printed in front of you,

00:20:22.303 --> 00:20:27.305
but you feed off of your musicians, you

00:20:25.005 --> 00:20:30.205
feed the musicians, and it's passed down

00:20:27.305 --> 00:20:33.005
generation to generation, hand to hand,

00:20:30.205 --> 00:20:35.505
heart to heart, and it is the living

00:20:33.005 --> 00:20:37.905
embodiment of American history and

00:20:35.505 --> 00:20:40.305
American musical history in these

00:20:37.905 --> 00:20:42.205
musicians. It's an American treasure,

00:20:40.305 --> 00:20:44.505
and Mr. President, you recognized that,

00:20:42.205 --> 00:20:46.505
you recognized that today. Mr. White,

00:20:44.505 --> 00:20:48.305
you heard that at the UFC fight and all

00:20:46.505 --> 00:20:50.505
of these other events, and it is our

00:20:48.305 --> 00:20:52.105
honor to serve in this incredibly

00:20:50.505 --> 00:20:54.205
special way.

00:20:52.105 --> 00:20:55.705
This is America's band.

00:20:54.205 --> 00:20:57.205
We want to bring it to every home, to

00:20:55.705 --> 00:20:59.805
every heart. The Marine Band can do

00:20:57.205 --> 00:21:01.705
something for everyone in our country,

00:20:59.805 --> 00:21:03.805
for every veteran, for every grieving

00:21:01.705 --> 00:21:05.605
family, for every music enthusiast, for

00:21:03.805 --> 00:21:07.805
every music student, for every music

00:21:05.605 --> 00:21:09.505
teacher. The Marine Band is there for

00:21:07.805 --> 00:21:11.505
you, just as we are for you, Mr.

00:21:09.505 --> 00:21:14.705
President. It is an honor to serve in

00:21:11.505 --> 00:21:17.705
this way, and we cannot thank you enough

00:21:14.705 --> 00:21:21.194
uh for this unbelievable reception here

00:21:17.705 --> 00:21:23.214
today. Thank you, Mr. President.

