00:33:18.513 --> 00:33:22.313
>> We're so proud to

00:33:20.013 --> 00:33:25.713
serve in our country in this way through

00:33:22.313 --> 00:33:28.313
our music as are so many so many around

00:33:25.713 --> 00:33:30.613
the world. Our next piece honors

00:33:28.313 --> 00:33:32.613
all service members, anyone who has

00:33:30.613 --> 00:33:36.313
served, all of those who have been

00:33:32.613 --> 00:33:38.413
impacted by service now or back in their

00:33:36.313 --> 00:33:40.913
families generations. This piece is

00:33:38.413 --> 00:33:43.313
called Let Freedom Ring and is a piece I

00:33:40.913 --> 00:33:45.013
composed based on the famous melody My

00:33:43.313 --> 00:33:46.713
Country, 'Tis of Thee.

00:33:45.013 --> 00:33:49.113
I focused on the lyric Land Where My

00:33:46.713 --> 00:33:50.613
Fathers Died because not a day goes by

00:33:49.113 --> 00:33:53.513
that we don't think of those who have

00:33:50.613 --> 00:33:55.413
sacrificed for us to be able to have the

00:33:53.513 --> 00:33:58.913
freedoms that we have today.

00:33:55.413 --> 00:33:58.913
This is Let Freedom Ring.

